# Transient artefacts. Everything listed here is regenerated by a documented command,
# so committing it would add bytes without adding evidence.

# --- rehearsal output: `to_run.py --mode smoke` rebuilds all of this in about a minute ---
results/raw_smoke/
results/summaries/smoke/
results/progress/smoke/
results/attempts/attempts_smoke.jsonl

# --- the real run's output, produced on the collaborator's machine, returned out of band ---
results/raw/*.json.gz
results/attempts/attempts.jsonl
results/progress/progress.jsonl
results/progress/state.json
results/progress/errors.jsonl
results/progress/provenance_*.json
results/logs/*.log

# --- caches: derived from the frozen constants, rebuilt on demand ---
# Patterned rather than by directory, so the directory itself stays in the tree.
results/cache/*.npy
results/cache/*.tmp

# --- DP shards: checkpoints, not results ---
# The 31^4 sweep runs five seeds at a time so a crash costs one block rather than the run; the
# shards exist only so it can be resumed. `ha_dp_merge.py` folds them into
# results/solver/ha_dynamic_equilibrium.json, which IS tracked. Committing both would ship the
# same numbers twice and invite them to disagree.
results/solver/_dp_shard_*.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
